.TH LUS-BUILD 1 "" "Lus" "Lus Manual"
.SH NAME
lus-build \- bundle a script and its modules into a standalone executable
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBlus build\fR [options] script
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bundles a script and the modules it requires into one executable, which runs on a machine that has neither \fBlus\fR nor the source files.
The command finds every \fBrequire\fR whose argument is a string literal.
Standalone executables describes the bundle.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o FILE\fR
Write the executable to \fBFILE\fR.
The default is the script name without its extension.
.TP
\fB\-P perm\fR, \fB\-\-pledge perm\fR
Grant a permission every time the executable runs.
.TP
\fB\-F name[=value]\fR, \fB\-\-flag name[=value]\fR
Define a build flag for the bundled code.
.TP
\fB\-\-include path[:alias]\fR
Bundle a module file or directory that no literal \fBrequire\fR names.
.TP
\fB\-\-aot\fR
Compile the program to machine code from a training run, and start the executable from \fBlus\-runtime\fR.
Compiling ahead of time describes it.
.TP
\fB\-\-train args\fR
The arguments of the training run of \fB\-\-aot\fR, separated by spaces.
.TP
\fB\-\-aot\-keep\-jit\fR
Start the executable from the running \fBlus\fR, which keeps the JIT and the compiler.
.TP
\fB\-\-aot\-static\fR
Compile ahead of time into the executable itself, for a system without executable memory.
.TP
\fB\-\-runtime FILE\fR
Start the executable from the runtime \fBFILE\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-link\-object FILE\fR
Link the executable from the link object \fBFILE\fR, keeping only what the program reaches.
Linking the runtime describes it.
.TP
\fB\-\-link\-all\fR
Keep every library function of the link object.
.TP
\fB\-\-link\-map FILE\fR
Write the size of each linked part of the runtime and what reached it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
The executable was written.
.TP
1
A module cannot be bundled or the executable cannot be written.
.TP
2
An option is malformed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lus (1)
.PP
The CLI page of the Lus manual, https://lus.dev/manual/cli#lus-build, has the same text with links to the rest of the manual.
